    '|b||Most economists now take a middle road. In Dani Rodrik''s version, economics is many models, and the skill is picking the right one for the case.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8160
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:91r6eh'
    '|a||An assumption is harmless if dropping it wouldn''t change the answer, and critical if it would.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1q0yvzg'
    '|a||How sure are we? On how much assumptions matter, the field is still split: contested.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1xu4sf8'
    '|a||So a false model can be the right tool, as long as the trees it leaves out aren''t the ones your question is about.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1ecil47'
    '|a||A traffic model treats every driver as identical and perfectly informed, and has predicted rush-hour jams well for ten years. What would Friedman say?':
